From d0857f539cda7f06d655eb167c1e20ef6d67ae49 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pierre-Hugues Husson <phh@phh.me>
Date: Wed, 26 Oct 2022 18:11:10 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] Support non-working BPF maps on old BPF-less kernel

[ported to Android 16: netbpfload/NetBpfLoad.cpp -> bpf/loader/NetBpfLoad.cpp
(rewritten upstream; fatal exit codes converted to failed flag),
BpfNetMapsReader.java -> NetworkStackBpfNetMaps.java + BpfNetMapsUtils.java,
staticlibs/native/bpf_headers -> bpf/headers, netd -> bpf/netd]

[verify fix: the A14 original converted every "Android X requires kernel Y"
check to failed=true (4.9 warn, 4.14 warn, 4.19 fatal). A16 made all of them
fatal (return 3/4/5/6); also convert return 4 (U/4.14), return 5 (V/4.19) and
return 6 (25Q2/5.4) so netbpfload never hard-fails on an old kernel, matching
the original intent. Line-count neutral, so patch 0005 offsets are unchanged.]

Change-Id: I3e01134a41155ee48335f40616472a2670860e48
---
